<svelte:head><title>FAQ | Smart Edit</title><meta name="description" content="Answers to common questions about the Smart Edit website: privacy, saved files, offline use, browsers and file size." /></svelte:head>
<article class="prose">
<h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
<details><summary>Are my files uploaded anywhere?</summary><p>No. Photos, scans and PDFs are processed in your browser on your own device, and nothing is sent to a server. There is no sign-up. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is Smart Edit free?</summary><p>Yes. All the tools on this website are free, with no sign-up and no limits on how many files you process.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I keep my results on the website?</summary><p>Yes. Tap <strong>Save</strong> next to a result to keep a copy in <a href="/library">My files</a>. Saved files stay in your browser on this device and are never uploaded. In My files you can search by file name or by words inside saved PDFs and text files (scanned PDFs without selectable text are found by name only). In another tool, choose <em>Choose from My files</em> to use one again. Clearing your browser’s site data deletes them, so download anything you can’t lose.</p></details>
<details><summary>Which browsers work?</summary><p>Current versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari on phones and computers. The scanner needs permission to use your camera; if you decline, you can add photos from your device instead.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does it work offline?</summary><p>After your first visit, most tools keep working without a connection. Extract text (OCR) needs a connection the first time you use each language, to download the text engine and language data.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is there a limit on file size?</summary><p>There is no upload limit because nothing is uploaded, but your device’s memory is. Very large PDFs or many big photos at once can stall on older phones. Try fewer or smaller files, or a lower resolution.</p></details>
<details><summary>What can the tools do?</summary><p>Scan documents with your camera or from photos; merge, split and reorganize PDFs; turn images into PDFs and PDF pages into images; compress and convert images and PDFs; edit images; and read text from pictures and PDFs (OCR).</p></details>
<details><summary>Which languages can it read?</summary><p>The website is in English. The text recognition tool can read English, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch, Russian, Turkish, Arabic, Hindi, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), Japanese and Korean.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can it open password-protected PDFs?</summary><p>Not yet. Remove the password in your PDF app first, then try again.</p></details>
<details><summary>A tool on this site gave me an error. What now?</summary><p>Very large files can run out of memory on some phones, so try fewer or smaller files. If it still fails, <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and tell us which tool and browser you used.</p></details>
</article>
